The '''Yam'rii''', also known as the '''Huk''', were an [[insectoid]] [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]] from the [[Wild Space]] [[planet]] [[Huk]], that were characterized by a triangular-shaped head poised on a long neck, large forward-facing [[eye]]s, and prominent upper [[limb]]s that were bent and held together at an angle.

==Biology and appearance==
The Yam'rii,<ref name="By the Numbers">{{SWKidsYouTube|series=Star Wars By the Numbers|text=Every Alien Species in the Original Trilogy|video=yHVzcCGUM9U|nolive=1}}</ref> also known as the Huk,<ref name="HC 8" /> were [[Color|green]]<ref name="Episode IV" /> or brown<ref name="Where's the Wookiee?" /> [[insectoid]]<ref name="HC 8" /> [[Sentience|sentient]] [[species]]<ref name="Episode IV" /> from the [[planet]]<ref name="Starships and Vehicles 55">{{ShipsandVehiclesCite|55|History of the Ship}}</ref> [[Huk]]<ref name="Rise" /> in [[Wild Space]],<ref name="Timelines">[[Star Wars Galaxy Map (poster)|''Star Wars'' Galaxy Map poster]]</ref> taller than 1.79 [[meter]]s,<ref name="Height" /> that resembled praying [[mantis]]es.<ref name="TBB Episode Guide" /> They had huge forward-facing [[eye]]s, a triangular-shaped head perched on a long neck, and noticeable upper [[limb]]s bent and held together at an angle.<ref name="Episode IV" />

==Society and culture==
Yam'rii were a greedy, technological, and destructive insectoid species,<ref name="The Separatists">{{EncyclopediaCite|The Separatists}}</ref> with the [[New Republic]]'s "[[Species From A to Z]]" profile theorizing the aliens were naturally violent and brutal.<ref name="Species From A to Z" /> One member of the species wore minimal [[clothing]], such as a cloth skirt.<ref name="Episode IV" />

==History==
The Yam'rii brutally overran numerous [[planet|worlds]] in the region, plundering their resources, [[Slavery|enslaving]] their populations,<ref name="The Separatists" /> and searching for strong opponents.<ref name="Species From A to Z" /> When the planet [[Kalee]] drew their interest, it resulted in a horrifying conquest of the native [[Kaleesh]] people.<ref name="The Separatists" /> What ensued was a [[Kaleesh-Yam'rii war|brutal struggle]] between the Yam'rii and the Kaleesh<ref name="Rise" /> in the form of an ongoing war. In [[time]],<ref name="The Separatists" /> the Kaleesh forces were led by Kaleesh [[warlord]]<ref name="HC 8" /> [[Grievous|Qymaen jai Sheelal]],<ref name="Build R2-D2 57">{{BuildR2Cite|57|Droid Directory}}</ref> later known as Grievous.<ref name="BDOWD">{{EncyclopediaCite|Battle Droids and Other Droids of War}}</ref> The Yam'rii were pushed back from Kalee to their own homeworld. When the Kaleesh invaded their world, they unexpectedly sought the [[Galactic Republic]] for assistance.<ref name="The Separatists" /> The Republic<ref name="Rise" /> and the [[Jedi Order]] intervened in the disastrous conflict<ref name="HC 8" /> and supported the Yam'rii against the Kaleesh.<ref name="Rise" /> They condemned, embargoed, and issued fines, resulting in hundreds of thousands of Kaleesh starving to [[death]].<ref name="The Separatists" /> At that moment, Grievous promised vengeance.<ref name="Rise" />

[[Sylar Saris]] was an [[insectoid]] [[bounty hunter]] active<ref name="BadTerritory">{{TBB|Bad Territory}}</ref> during or after [[18 BBY]]<ref name="TBBS3Date">{{TBBDate|308}}</ref> who resembled the Yam'rii species. He was known as "The Slayer of [[Ordo Eris]]" and had become highly wanted after performing several bounties on behalf of the [[Haxion Brood]] crime syndicate. The bounty on Saris was eventually claimed by fellow bounty hunter [[Fennec Shand]], who was aided by former [[clone commando]]s [[Hunter]] and [[Wrecker]].<ref name="BadTerritory" /> Saris supposedly belonged to a [[Sylar Saris' species|subspecies]] of Yam'rii.<ref name="TBB Episode Guide" /> This [[subspecies]] was capable of spitting [[Color|green]]<ref name="BadTerritory" /> [[acid]]<ref name="BTAD">{{TBB|Bad Territory}} {{AD|Disney+}}</ref> out of their [[mouth]]s.<ref name="BadTerritory" />

In [[1 BBY]],<ref name="IV Date">{{FilmDate|IV|1}}</ref> one Yam'rii was present in [[Chalmun]]'s [[Chalmun's Spaceport Cantina|cantina]] in [[Mos Eisley]], [[Tatooine]], on the [[Standard day|day]] [[Luke Skywalker]] and [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]] met [[Han Solo]] and [[Chewbacca]].<ref name="Episode IV" />

An entry on Yam'rii was included in "Species From A to Z," a survival compendium sent out by [[Carson Teva]] during the [[New Republic Era]].<ref name="Species From A to Z" />

==Behind the scenes==
Known only as "[[Wikipedia:Praying mantis|Praying Mantis]]" during the shooting of [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']], this alien puppet was operated by actor [[Jack Purvis]], who also played other roles in the [[original trilogy]], including the [[Jawa]] chief, the [[Ugnaught]] chief, and [[Teebo]] the [[Ewok]].<ref name="KK DB">{{DB|character|kitikkeedkak|Keed'kak, Kitik}}</ref> During one day of shooting, his son [[Andy Purvis]] operated the puppet.<ref name="Andy Purvis">{{InsiderCite|218|Andy Purvis: A Bug's Life}}</ref>

[[File:PossibleSenatorsHostageChisisArt.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Concept art for a Yam'rii senator.]]
The Yam'rii first appeared in the [[1977]] film ''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope''.<ref name="Episode IV" /> The species was first [[canon]]ically identified in the [[2019]] ''[[Star Wars By the Numbers]]'' video "Every Alien Species in the Original Trilogy".<ref name="By the Numbers" /> In the [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]] continuity, the [[Yam'rii/Legends|Yam'rii]] were a [[Insectoid/Legends|insectoid]] [[Sentience/Legends|sentient]] [[Species/Legends|species]] with a praying [[Mantis/Legends|mantis]] characteristics first identified in the ''[[Premiere Limited]]'' base set of the [[Star Wars Customizable Card Game|''Star Wars'' Customizable Card Game]], which was released in [[December]] [[1995]]. The cards also identified the individual seen in ''A New Hope'' as [[Kitik Keed'kak]].<ref name="KK CCG">{{CCG|set=Premiere Limited|cardname=Kitik Keed'kak}}</ref> At one point Yam'rii were considered for the role of a senator in [[Star Wars: The Clone Wars]] episode [[Hostage Crisis]]. [[Russell G. Chong]] created concept art for a Morseerian senator.{{WebCite|url=https://www.artrgcportfolio.com/starwarstheclonewars|text=Star Wars The Clone Wars Lucasfilm Animation Ltd.|author=Russel Chong|archivedate=20251203011921}}

